    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d270">

                <pb facs="0319" n="1053" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1053"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lima,
                                Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-08-29"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 29, 1895</hi></date>. (Received
                        September 24.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 237.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Sir: Referring to the claim of the Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, I have
                    the honor to report that as the ordinary session of <pb facs="0320" n="1054"
                        xml:id="pg1054"/> Congress opens to-morrow, I have this day placed a note in
                    the hands of his excellency Senor Manuel Candamo, minister for foreign relations
                    of Peru, regarding this long-pending claim of citizens of the United States upon
                    the Peruvian Government, and respectfully asking his excellency to have the
                    claim presented to this Congress for its early consideration, as per my inclosed
                    note.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d270-a1.xml" xpointer="d270-a1"/>
            </div>
